IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cccfa-types`
IMPORT `cccfa-dates`
IMPORT `cccfa-cancellation`
IMPORT `cccfa-interest`
IMPORT `cccfa-damages`

-- Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For a consumer credit contract: is it high-cost, may it be entered into,
--    how much more may be charged, is a cancellation effective and by when,
--    and what statutory damages follow its breaches?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Credit position` HAS
    `high-cost`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `may be entered into`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `further costs of borrowing recoverable`            IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `cancellation effective`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `last day to cancel`                                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `statutory damages`                                 IS A NUMBER

@ref ss 27-29, 45C-45I, 89
@export default A consumer credit contract's position under the Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 (NZ): whether it is high-cost (s 45C) and may be entered into on its date (ss 45F, 45G, 45I); for a high-cost contract, the further costs of borrowing recoverable under the first-advance cap (s 45E); whether the debtor's cancellation is effective and the last day to cancel (ss 27-29); and the statutory damages for simultaneous breaches (s 89). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN h IS A `High-cost facts`  @desc The rates, the debtor's other high-cost contracts, the defence, compound interest, the first advance and costs so far
      d IS A DATE  @desc The day the contract is entered into
      c IS A Cancellation  @desc The disclosure and cancellation facts
      breaches IS A LIST OF Breach  @desc Any breaches at or about the same time
GIVETH A `Credit position`
`the credit position for` h `, entered on` d `, cancellation` c `, breaches` breaches MEANS
    `Credit position` WITH
        `high-cost`                                 IS highCost
        `may be entered into`                       IS `the high-cost contract may be entered into` h `on` d
        `further costs of borrowing recoverable`    IS IF highCost THEN JUST (`the further costs of borrowing recoverable under` h) ELSE NOTHING
        `cancellation effective`                    IS `the cancellation is effective` c
        `last day to cancel`                        IS `the last day to cancel` c
        `statutory damages`                         IS `the statutory damages for the simultaneous breaches` breaches
    WHERE
        highCost MEANS `is a high-cost consumer credit contract` h
